# Shell scripts must be checked out with LF endings, whatever the developer's
# core.autocrlf says. With autocrlf=true — the Windows default, and set globally on at
# least one machine here — a checkout rewrites release.sh with CRLF, and the shebang then
# fails as `env: bash\r: No such file or directory`. The repository stores LF either way;
# this is about what lands in the working tree.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the files CI and the release pipeline parse.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
